                                    <h2>FAQs</h2>
<h3>Should a new D2C brand start with SEO or PPC?</h3>
<p><strong>PPC for revenue + SEO foundation from day 30.</strong> 85% PPC initially, 15% SEO foundation (technical + content cluster planning). By month 6, shift to 60/40. By month 18, shift to 50/50 or further into SEO.</p>
<h3>How long does SEO take to deliver D2C revenue?</h3>
<p><strong>First meaningful organic traffic in 3&ndash;6 months. ROI break-even around month 7&ndash;9. Compounding revenue from month 9 onward.</strong> Anyone promising 4-week SEO is gaming a metric.</p>
<h3>What ROAS does SEO deliver vs PPC at maturity?</h3>
<p><strong>PPC: 3&times;&ndash;7&times; ROAS, capped by spend.</strong> <strong>SEO: 8&times;&ndash;15&times; effective ROAS at maturity (12+ months in)</strong> because traffic is &ldquo;free&rdquo; once the content + ranking foundation is built.</p>
<h3>What is AEO and GEO?</h3>
<p><strong>AEO (Answer Engine Optimization)</strong>: optimising content for answer-engine citations (ChatGPT, Perplexity, Google AI Overviews, Bing Copilot). <strong>GEO (Generative Engine Optimization)</strong>: the broader umbrella including AI search ranking + brand-mention signals. Both required for 2026 organic strategy.</p>
<h3>Should I cut PPC once SEO is working?</h3>
<p><strong>No.</strong> Even at 80% SEO traffic, keep 20&ndash;30% PPC for: brand defense, new-product launches, flash sales, geographic expansion, retargeting, and high-intent comparison queries. PPC remains the speed lever.</p>
<h3>How much should I budget for SEO + AEO in 2026?</h3>
<p><strong>&#8377;60K&ndash;&#8377;2L/month for growth-stage D2C; &#8377;2L&ndash;&#8377;5L/month for scale.</strong> Includes technical SEO, content cluster (4&ndash;8 articles/month), AEO/GEO optimisation, schema, link-building. Below &#8377;60K/month it&rsquo;s not real SEO.</p>


